  "question": {
    "text": "The activation energy, rate-constant and Arrhenius parameters of a chemical reaction at 25<sup>o</sup>C are 104.4 KJ mol<sup>-1</sup>, 3.0 x 10<sup>-4</sup> s<sup>-1</sup>, 6.0 x 10<sup>14</sup> s<sup>-1</sup> respectively. The value of rate-constant in <math> <mrow> <msup> <mi>s</mi> <mrow> <mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math> at <math> <mrow> <mtext>T</mtext> <mo>→</mo> <mo>∞</mo> </mrow> </math> is&nbsp; &nbsp;(write your answer by dividing by 10<sup>14</sup>)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math> <mrow> <mtext>k</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>A</mtext> <mo>·</mo> <msup> <mtext>e</mtext> <mrow> <mo>-</mo> <mtext>Ea</mtext> <mo>/</mo> <mtext>RT</mtext> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp; (Arrhenius equation)<br /><br />As <math> <mrow> <mtext>T</mtext> <mo>→</mo> <mo>∞</mo> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><mat> <mrow> <mtext>k</mtext> <mo>→</mo> <mo>A</mo> </mrow><br /><br />i.e., <math> <mrow> <mtext>k</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>A</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mn>6</mn> <mo>×</mo> <mn>1</mn> <msup> <mn>0</mn> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </msup> <msup> <mo>sec</mo> <mn>-1</mn> </msup> </mrow> </math> </mat>"
  }
